diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 16d5d5ba..d1186168 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -119,6 +119,7 @@ over SSH standard streams. There is no HTTP service, listening port, Python runt
 The Linux collector reuses the native measurement core, including omp parsing and parent/child deduplication. The
 remote host has its own identity and history, separate from local usage. A disconnected host is shown offline with
 stale data, not as idle or zero usage; reconnection replaces its snapshot and history rather than adding them again.
+On macOS, cached history remains stale after reconnecting until a new history frame arrives, even if live snapshots resume.
 Fields absent from logs are unknown. Live rates inferred from recent completed responses are estimates; completed
 response rates use the logged duration. In particular omp commonly writes a response when it completes, so remote
 monitoring cannot measure per-token streaming speed or infer an unrecorded time to first token. End-to-end speed includes
